- Google's Transparency Report and all `support.google.com` (CAPTCHA); Google's Android backup E2EE primary text.
- Threema's Q1-2023 rebuttal post; USENIX's own Threema page (403).
- Fusion/Splinter psychiatrist article body (URL + date confirmed, host dead, archive.org blocked).
- Le Monde Oct-2024 bodyguard piece body; Strava's own heatmap scale figures (Medium 403); The Pillar's methodology (paywalled).
- Bumble 2023 follow-up (404); Grindr/Kyoto 2016 metre figures (PDF-only).
- Briar's funded 2023 audit; SimpleX's announced early-2025 implementation assessment; VeilidChat's routing-context configuration (GitLab blob search needs auth); `veilid.com/chat/known-issues/` and `/chat/privacy/` (both 404).

## Things that appear not to exist at all

- Any measured deployment or adoption figure for GNS/GNUnet.
- Any published discussion of CRDT actor IDs as a deanonymization channel (Automerge, Yjs, or the literature).
- Any measured study of device attestation as a fingerprinting/linkage channel (0 arXiv hits).
- Any measured accuracy figure for IP-based cross-device/household graphs.
- Any measured study of backup metadata as a cross-persona linkage vector.
- Any measured study of passively linking N pseudonyms on one device by correlated activity timing. The "user identity linkage" literature is graph-, content-, and GPS-based, and most of it reports only improvements over baselines rather than absolute rates — it is not calibrated for threat modelling. *Careless Whisper* gets there actively instead.
- Any NIP on multiple identities, personas, or account switching (whole repo grepped).
- Any independent security audit of Cwtch; any academic cryptanalysis of SimpleX or of Session.
- Any measured LinkedIn PYMK leak, Instagram "Suggested for you" finsta outing, or Blind deanonymization incident.
